Uno R package -- copyright and licensing of bundled code
========================================================

Scope. This file describes the SOURCE package (the tarball). The bundled
sources under inst/uno/ and inst/HiGHS/ are compiled into the package library
at installation time and are then removed from the installed package (see
.Rinstignore), so an installed copy of this file is self-contained: it quotes
each copyright statement and names the license, and the MIT text referred to
below is the one in the package's own LICENSE file (identical to the MIT text
every bundled MIT component carries).

The Uno R package itself -- the R code, src/uno_binding.cpp, src/dmumps_shim.c,
src/dmumps_shim.h, the configure scripts, inst/build_*.sh, tools/, the vignette
and the documentation -- is Copyright (c) 2026 Balasubramanian Narasimhan and
is released under the MIT License (file LICENSE).

For convenience the package builds and statically links the following
third-party libraries from bundled source. Every bundled component is under a
permissive, MIT-compatible license (MIT, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0, zlib, or the
Boost Software License 1.0); none is copyleft.


